upd("n644", text="Ambrose, *De fide* I. The Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 9 c. 2, cites it as ‘Ambrosius in I libro De Trinitate’: *si pater prius erat… generationis accessione mutatus est. Sed avertat Deus hanc amentiam*. The *in littera* is the Lombard's text, *Sent.* I d. 9.", append="[Checked: Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 9 c. 2 (Quaracchi via SCTA): ‘Si enim ante Deus, postea Pater fuit, utique generationis accessione mutatus est. Sed avertat Deus hanc amentiam’. Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 9 q. 1 (Wadding/Vivès via SCTA): ‘Ambrosius 1. de Trin. cap. 6. et ponitur in littera’. Verified. The chapter is corrected from c. 4 to c. 2.]", status="verified")
upd("n645", append="[Checked: Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 9 q. 1 (Wadding/Vivès via SCTA): ‘auctoritas Hilarii in littera: Inter gignere et gigni nullum est medium’. Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 9 c. 4 (Quaracchi via SCTA) cites Hilary, *De Trin.* XII, on eternal nativity (‘ab aeterno auctore aeterna nativitas est’), and VII. The exact words *inter gignere et gigni* were not found in the Lombard’s d. 9, and Hilary’s text was not opened.]", status="probable")
upd("n646", append="[Checked: Wadding/Vivès via SCTA, *Ord.* I d. 5, the question whether the Son is generated from the substance of the Father. The cross-reference is internal and consistent with section 030. Verified.]", status="verified")
upd("n647", append="[Checked: Aquinas, *ST* I q. 42 a. 3 co. (Corpus Thomisticum): ‘In divinis autem dicitur principium secundum originem, absque prioritate’, i.e. *ordo naturae* without priority. Verified.]", status="verified")
upd("n648", append="[Checked: Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 19 c. 1 (Quaracchi via SCTA) quotes ‘Augustinus in libro De fide ad Petrum’: ‘Nullus horum alium aut praecedit aeternitate, aut excedit magnitudine, aut superat potestate’. This supports A’s *aut* against B’s *et*. Fulgentius’s own text was not opened. The sentence is located via the Lombard. Verified.]", status="verified")
upd("n649", append="[Checked on augustinus.it: *In Io. tract.* 99.5 has ‘et audivit, et audit, et audiet: quia … hoc est illi audire quod scire, et scire illi hoc est quod esse. Ab illo igitur audivit, audit, et audiet a quo est’. Verified for 99.5. Tract. 18 (§ 10) discusses hearing and seeing in the Word, not the Spirit’s hearing. Gorris’s ‘omelia 18’ is a parallel at best.]", status="verified")
upd("n650", text="Peter Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 8 c. 1: of God properly only *est* is said, not *fuit* or *erit*. The Master's discussion of tenses applied to God.", append="[Checked: Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 8 c. 1 (Quaracchi via SCTA) quotes Augustine ‘Super Iohannem’: ‘Cum de sempiterna re proprie dicatur est, secundum nos bene dicitur fuit et erit’. Verified. In Quaracchi this is c. 1.]", status="verified")
